        "description": "Retrieves policy excerpts from a vector database and builds a prompt for LLM to rank top 5 health plans.\n\nThis node creates a prompt for an LLM to shortlist the five best health insurance policies for a user. It first parses the user profile string to extract key attributes (sum insured, chronic condition, maternity, wellness, OPD) and constructs a retrieval query that combines these terms with “health insurance policy” and “policy wording benefits”. The node queries the insurance vector database with top_k=30 to obtain relevant policy excerpts, then inserts these together with the user profile and a scorecard (containing rubrics, weights, and hard filters) into a structured prompt. The LLM is instructed to apply hard filters, compute seven criterion scores (0‑10) for each policy, apply profile‑adaptive weights, drop ineligible policies, and output exactly the top five in a strict TOP_5_READY format. This ensures a data‑driven, transparent shortlist based on both user needs and policy attributes.",
