  "variables": [
    {
      "id": "2e82740e-17d4-4212-a3e2-c3e41d7d42c9",
      "name": "health_insurance_scorecard",
      "resourceType": "variable",
      "description": "",
      "components": {
        "bbdca5a7": {
          "type": "string",
          "value": "# HEALTH INSURANCE SCORECARD - v1.0  ## RUBRICS (0-10 per criterion)  ### 1. Chronic / PED coverage Base from PED waiting months:   0       → 10   1-12    → 7   13-24   → 5   25-36   → 3   37-48   → 2   >48     → 1 Bonuses:   +3 if chronic_day1 == Y   +1 if opd_chronic == Y   +1 if specific_disease_waiting_months <= 12 Cap at 10.  ### 2. Senior citizen suitability Age band (max entry age):   >=80   → 4   70-79  → 3   65-69  → 2   <65    → 0 +2 if lifelong_renewal == Y Co-pay senior pct: 0%→4, 10%→3, 20%→2, 30%→1, >30%→0 Sublimits: none→+2, some→+1, many→0 Cap at 10.  ### 3. Maternity cover Waiting months:   no_maternity → 0   <=12         → 4   13-24        → 3   25-36        → 2   37-48        → 1 Normal + C-section sum (% of SI): >5%→3, 2-5%→2, <2%→1 +2 if newborn_day1 == Y +1 if vaccination_cover == Y Cap at 10.  ### 4. Cashless network (network density + insurer settlement) Network score (hospitals):   >15k →5, 10–15k→4, 5–10k→3, 2–5k→2, <2k→1 Settlement bonus (CSR by count):   ≥99%→3, 95–99%→2, 90–95%→1, <90%→0 +2 if direct_inhouse_claims == Y Cap at 10.  ### 5. Preventive care annual_checkup==Y → +3 wellness_rewards==Y → +2 telemedicine==Y → +1 opd_general==Y → +2 pre_hosp_days ≥60 → +1 post_hosp_days ≥180 → +1 Cap at 10.  ### 6. Approval rate (Claim Settlement Ratio by count) CSR mapping:   ≥99% →10, 97–99%→9, 95–97%→8, 92–95%→7, 90–92%→6,   85–90%→5, 80–85%→4, 75–80%→3, <75%→2  ### 7. Hospital network size (hospitals count) >20,000 →10, 15–20k→9, 10–15k→8, 7–10k→6, 5–7k→5, 3–5k→4, 1–3k→3, <1k→2  ## WEIGHTS (base + user‑adaptive) Weights sum to 100. Use the table below.  Criterion                | Base | Senior60+ | YoungFamily | ChronicPatient | FrequentTraveler -------------------------|------|-----------|-------------|----------------|----------------- chronic                  | 15   | 20        | 5           | 35             | 10 senior_citizen           | 10   | 30        | 0           | 5              | 5 maternity                | 10   | 0         | 30          | 5              | 5 cashless                 | 20   | 15        | 15          | 15             | 30 preventive               | 5    | 5         | 10          | 5              | 5 approval_rate            | 25   | 20        | 25          | 25             | 20 hospital_network         | 15   | 10        | 15          | 10             | 25  ## PROFILE SELECTION LOGIC Use the first matching rule: - if age >= 60 → Senior60+ - elif chronic_condition == true → ChronicPatient - elif marital_status == married and planning_family == true → YoungFamily - elif travel_freq in [\"monthly\", \"weekly\"] → FrequentTraveler - else → Base  ## HARD FILTERS (must be applied before scoring) - If chronic_condition == true: require (chronic_day1 == Y OR ped_waiting_months <= 12) - If age >= 65: require (entry_age_max >= age AND lifelong_renewal == Y) - If want_maternity == true: require (maternity_available == Y AND maternity_waiting_months <= 24) - If sum_insured_min specified: require max_sum_insured_lakhs >= sum_insured_min (convert both to numeric)  ## POLICY ATTRIBUTES TABLE Columns: insurer | product | ped_waiting_months | chronic_day1 | opd_chronic | entry_age_max | lifelong_renewal | copay_senior_pct | senior_sublimits | maternity_available | maternity_waiting_months | maternity_normal_amount | maternity_csection_amount | newborn_day1 | vaccination_cover | annual_checkup | wellness_rewards | telemedicine | opd_general | pre_hosp_days | post_hosp_days | max_sum_insured_lakhs  HDFC Ergo | Optima Secure | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 0 | none | N | 0 | 0 | 0 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 60 | 180 | 200 HDFC Ergo | Optima Wellbeing Add-on | 0 | N | N | 65 | Y | 0 | none | N | 0 | 0 | 0 | N | N | N | N | Y | Y | 0 | 0 | 0 Star Health | Star Comprehensive | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 36 | 30000 | 40000 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | 60 | 90 | 100 Star Health | Star Health Assure | 36 | N | N | 75 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 36 | 30000 | 40000 | Y | N | Y | Y | Y | N | 60 | 90 | 200 Star Health | Senior Citizens Red Carpet | 12 | N | N | 75 | Y | 30 | many | N | 0 | 0 | 0 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 30 | 60 | 25 Niva Bupa | ReAssure | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 24 | 50000 | 60000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | N | 90 | 180 | 100 Niva Bupa | ReAssure 2.0 | 36 | N | N | 99 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 24 | 50000 | 60000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | N | 90 | 180 | 1000 Niva Bupa | ReAssure 3.0 | 36 | N | N | 99 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 24 | 50000 | 60000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | N | 60 | 180 | 1000 ICICI Lombard | Complete Health Insurance iHealth | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 15000 | 25000 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 30 | 60 | 50 ICICI Lombard | Complete Health Insurance Health Shield | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 15000 | 25000 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 30 | 60 | 50 ICICI Lombard | Complete Health Insurance Health Elite | 36 | N | Y | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 25000 | 40000 | N | N | Y | N | Y | Y | 60 | 180 | 300 ICICI Lombard | Complete Health Insurance | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 15000 | 25000 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 30 | 60 | 50 Care | Care Supreme | 36 | N | N | 99 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 24 | 50000 | 60000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | N | 30 | 60 | 300 Aditya Birla | Activ One NXT | 36 | Y | Y | 99 | Y | 0 | none | Y | 24 | 75000 | 100000 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | 30 | 180 | 200 Aditya Birla | Activ Health | 48 | Y | Y | 99 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 24 | 75000 | 100000 | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | Y | 30 | 60 | 200 Tata AIG | MediCare Premier | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 30000 | 40000 | Y | Y | Y | N | Y | N | 60 | 180 | 300 Tata AIG | MediCare | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | Y | 36 | 15000 | 25000 | N | N | Y | N | Y | N | 60 | 180 | 100 Tata AIG | MediCare LITE | 36 | N | N | 65 | Y | 20 | none | N | 0 | 0 | 0 | N | Y | Y | Y | Y | N | 60 | 180 | 25 New India Assurance | Senior Citizen Mediclaim | 18 | N | N | 80 | Y | 20 | many | N | 0 | 0 | 0 | N | N | Y | N | N | N | 30 | 60 | 5  ## MARKET STATS TABLE Columns: insurer | csr_by_count_pct | network_hospitals | direct_inhouse_claims  Star Health | 86.4 | 20000 | Y HDFC Ergo | 97 | 13000 | N Niva Bupa | 93 | 10000 | N ICICI Lombard | 95 | 6500 | N Care | 87 | 24000 | N Aditya Birla | 95.5 | 11000 | N Tata AIG | 94 | 7200 | N ManipalCigna | 91 | 8500 | N New India Assurance | 93.5 | 3000 | N Oriental Insurance | 90 | 3500 | N United India | 88 | 3200 | N National Insurance | 89 | 3500 | N Go Digit | 96.5 | 7000 | N  ## FINAL SCORES Quality = Σ(weight x criterion_score) / 10   (0-100) Value  = Quality / (annual_premium_in_thousands)  (use user's premium if known)  ## NOTES - Always apply hard filters before scoring. - For missing attributes, assume conservative values (e.g., no bonus). - Output only the top 5 policies with their quality scores.",
